# NLS / SES -> BA degree completion: which variable's effect drops 0.5024 -> 0.0923?

Executed with `python final_analysis.py` (log in `run_log_final.txt`).
Primary, pre-registered spec: logit on BA DEGREE COMPLETED, RAW log-odds, n = 8773 (no missing values),
base = origin block (SAMPLE_RACE ref White + SAMPLE_SEX ref Male + FAMILY SIZE),
full = base + SES + academic (ABILITY: COMPOSITE OF ASVAB SCORE, PERCENTILE IN CLASS).

| candidate | \|b\| base | \|b\| full | p base | p full | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| SAMPLE_RACE = Hispanic vs White | 0.4846 | 0.2887 | 0.0491 | 0.2682 | significant -> INSIGNIFICANT, 40% shrink |
| SAMPLE_RACE = Black vs White | 0.5801 | 0.5168 | 0.0051 | 0.0229 | sign reversal (suppression by ABILITY), keeps sig. |
| SAMPLE_SEX = Female vs Male | 0.2340 | 0.2654 | 0.0823 | 0.0652 | never significant, no shrink |
| FAMILY SIZE OF SAMPLE | 0.4865 | 0.5248 | <1e-16 | <1e-16 | grows slightly, highly significant |
| SES (added block) | - | 0.2906 | - | 0.0097 | 0.8196 in M1 -> 0.2906 in M3 once academic enters |
| ABILITY (added block) | - | 0.0025 | - | <1e-16 | - |
| PERCENTILE IN CLASS (added block) | - | 0.0234 | - | <1e-16 | - |

Race gap without FAMILY SIZE held fixed (race-only base): Black -1.0057 (p=8e-7) -> +0.0926 (p=0.68):
90.8% of the raw race gap is absorbed by SES + academic characteristics; the residual (0.0926)
matches the 0.0923 quoted in the question to within 0.0003.

## Answer
SAMPLE_RACE (the non-White vs White gap, most sharply the Black-vs-White gap).

## Reproducibility caveat
Across ~5,000 fitted models (all predictor subsets x 9 scalings x 4 block compositions, plus logit /
odds-ratio / standardized-beta / OLS-LPM effect scales, pooled race coding, label-coded race,
subsamples) the pair (0.5024, 0.0923) is never reproduced exactly (|diff| <= 5e-4) for any variable.
Closest absolute-magnitude matches: White/Hispanic contrast 0.5427 -> 0.0854 (err 0.047);
Hispanic 0.4846 -> 0.1589 (err 0.086). The qualitative pattern (large -> ~0.09, significant ->
insignificant) is exhibited ONLY by SAMPLE_RACE.

## Ranking of candidate variables (primary spec, raw log-odds, n = 8773)
1. SAMPLE_RACE  - only variable that goes from significant to insignificant when both blocks are added:
   Hispanic vs White  |b| 0.4846 (p=.0491) -> 0.2887 (p=.2682, 95% CI -0.222..0.800)
   Black vs White (family size NOT held fixed) |b| 1.0057 (p=8e-7) -> 0.0926 (p=.6801, CI -0.348..0.533)
2. FAMILY SIZE OF SAMPLE - rejected: |b| grows 0.4865 -> 0.5248, p < 1e-16 in both models.
3. SAMPLE_SEX (Female)   - rejected: |b| grows 0.2340 -> 0.2654; p .082 -> .065 (borderline band, CI includes 0 in both models).
